---
title: Find the orders that need action
order: 4
summary: A status dashboard that says everything with colour and nothing with words.
scenario: It is Monday morning on the customer service desk. Your manager wants to know how many orders need chasing before the 10 o'clock stand-up. The dashboard uses a traffic light system that everybody says is obvious.
tasks:
  - Count the orders that need action and type the number in. Do not read the table row by row, do it the way you would at 9am.
  - Now change the colour vision setting and count again without reloading.
  - Try the greyscale setting, then imagine this printed out or read over the phone.
time: 8 minutes
barrier: Colour used as the only way of telling things apart
criterion: WCAG 2.2 &mdash; <a href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/use-of-color.html">1.4.1 Use of Color</a>
script: colour.js
---

